   "notes": "Born-digital typed filing, Rachel Anne Kahler, Wasatch County Council Seat A, Republican, Heber City. Primary Report marked with a typed 'X' beside the box; initialled RK twice; signed 6/16/2026. THIS IS THE PAGE-3 CONTINUATION SPECIMEN, and it continues in TWO different ways at once: (1) Table B's TOTAL row spills onto page 3 exactly as the brief warns — page 2's Table B frame ends with no TOTAL, and 2,854.92 prints at the top of page 3; and (2) Table A overflows its 12 printed slots, so the filer used the last slot to write 'See additional information below' and appended an UNHEADERED 12-row continuation table lower on page 3, whose columns are date | name | amount | (empty) | 'Donation'. Both continuations were confirmed by the printed totals, not assumed. The 'See additional information below' slot is a POINTER, not a ledger line — no date, no amount — so it is not emitted as a row; the rows it points to are (line_no 12-23 below). Amount column read POSITIONALLY on both blocks: on p2 the Amount cell holds bare integers (200, 500, 50 ...) while the trailing In-Kind column holds the word 'Donation'; on the p3 block the money is in the third column ($500.00 style) with 'Donation' again trailing. Per gate (g) the In-Kind cell here is a DESCRIPTION of a cash gift, not an in-kind good, so in_kind is false throughout with the cell quoted. Rows are not in date order in either block (p3 runs 5/15/2026 before 5/9/2026). Row 1 is the candidate's own $200 self-contribution. Form prints no address column, so donor_city/donor_state are blank by design. NOTE for the wave lead: Kahler's MARCH 2026 filing is this module's zero-glyph calibration specimen (both totals printed as the written word 'zero'); this JUNE filing is a different, fully-populated report and shares nothing with it but the filer."
